    "body": "## Goal\nAgree on **one** interface from Karan's website evidence / JS1–JS10 output to Patricio's deterministic Python inference; prevent two incompatible fact schemas.\n\n**Owner lane:** INTEGRATION — requires review by both Karan and Patricio before change.\n\n## Design constraints\n- A website quote verifies **attribution**, not truth, a manufacturing process, or sourcing demand.\n- Product, assembly, component, material, evidence references, review state, and inferred roles must be distinguishable.\n- JS5 (process requirement) must not be confused with JS6 (manufacturer's capability).\n- JS7 potential fit must not become a declared RFQ or procurement requirement.\n- The Python prototype's exact field names may differ: inspect those before finalizing a schema.\n- No private research or real supplier exports in the public repository.\n\n## Acceptance\n- [ ] Review Patricio's actual Python input/output JSON.\n- [ ] Publish one canonical versioned schema and sanitized positive/negative fixtures.\n- [ ] Both sides write an adapter, rather than rewriting each other's engine.\n- [ ] Tests fail on missing review status, source attribution, schema version, or invalid company/component references.\n- [ ] Both owners sign off on the schema version before implementation.\n\n**Starting point:** `contracts/proposals/evidence-to-engineering.v0.schema.json` is a **proposal only**, not a frozen engine API.\n",
